text+='| Kernel subject START/EXIT | Subject PID, CreateTime, ProcessSequenceNumber, parent sequence, image; ETW QPC | Extended header key not captured; emitter identity must not be confused with payload subject |\n| Native owned PE tracer | Owned child PID + creation FILETIME, PE-entry QPC, exit; parent launcher identity | Not automatically a helper/conhost PE identity |\n| Retained Windows handle | GetProcessId, GetProcessTimes creation/exit, QueryFullProcessImageName, wait signal/exit code | Numeric handle is local, not a portable instance key; no application events synthesized |\n| CIM START/STOP | PID/name, parent PID where present, event generation TIME_CREATED; callback/enqueue QPC separately | No subject CreateTime or sequence; STOP parent may be zero; cannot resolve every reuse case |\n| Supported process snapshot | PID, parent PID, SequenceNumber, image name | Only current snapshot; not history; sequence equivalence to ETW NOT established |\n| Cleanup checker | Requires verified creation/sequence/lineage plus exit proof | Name/PID absence alone insufficient; ambiguity remains fatal |\n\n'
text+='The supported SystemBasicProcessInformation query was tested on Windows 10.0.26200.0 (UBR9457); SDK information class252 and public structure were inspected. Two snapshots per owned suspended process returned stable sequences for eight distinct instances. No administrator privilege was required for these owned-process checks. Suspension makes these fixtures unsuitable for measuring natural startup latency. Version/capability rejection must remain fail closed. ETW collection elevation was not exercised here.\n\n'
text+='Primary references: [process handles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/procthread/process-handles-and-identifiers), [documented snapshot API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winternl/nf-winternl-ntquerysysteminformation), [ETW enable properties](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/evntrace/ns-evntrace-enable_trace_parameters), [CIM START schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/desktop/krnlprov/win32-processstarttrace), [QPC clock guidance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/sysinfo/acquiring-high-resolution-time-stamps). A second ETW subscription is a separate transport, not an independent event source.\n\n'
